.TH "FLOX\-CONFIG" "1" "" "" "Flox User Manuals"
.SH NAME
flox\-config \- view and set configuration options
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
flox [<general\-options>] config
     [\-l |
      \-r |
      \-\-set <key> <string> |
      \-\-delete=<key>]
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without any flags or when \f[CR]\-l\f[R] is passed,
\f[CR]flox config\f[R] shows all options with their computed value.
.PP
Config values are read from the following sources in order of descending
priority:
.IP "1." 3
Environment variables.
All config options may be set by prefixing with \f[CR]FLOX_\f[R] and
using \f[CR]SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE\f[R].
For example, \f[CR]disable_metrics\f[R] may be set with
\f[CR]FLOX_DISABLE_METRICS=true\f[R].
.IP "2." 3
User customizations from \f[CR]$FLOX_CONFIG_DIR/flox.toml\f[R] if set,
otherwise \f[CR]flox/flox.toml\f[R] in \f[CR]$XDG_CONFIG_HOME\f[R] or
any of \f[CR]$XDG_CONFIG_DIRS\f[R], wherever it is found first.
.IP "3." 3
System settings from \f[CR]/etc/flox.toml\f[R] or
\f[CR]FLOX_SYSTEM_CONFIG_DIR/flox.toml\f[R].
.IP "4." 3
\f[CR]flox\f[R] provided defaults.
.PP
\f[CR]flox config\f[R] commands that mutate configuration always write
to the user config file determined in step 2.
.SS Key Format
\f[CR]<key>\f[R] supports dot\-separated queries for nested values, for
example:
.IP
.EX
flox config \-\-set \(aqtrusted_environments.\(dqowner/name\(dq\(aq trust
.EE
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Config Options
.TP
\f[CR]\-l\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-list\f[R]
List the current values of all options.
.TP
\f[CR]\-r\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-reset\f[R]
Reset all options to their default values without confirmation.
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-set <key> <string>\f[R]
Set \f[CR]<key> = <string>\f[R] for a config key
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-delete <key>\f[R]
Delete config key
.SS General Options
.TP
\f[CR]\-h\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-help\f[R]
Prints help information.
.PP
The following options can be passed when running any \f[CR]flox\f[R]
subcommand but must be specified \f[I]before\f[R] the subcommand.
.TP
\f[CR]\-v\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-verbose\f[R]
Increase logging verbosity.
Invoke multiple times for increasing detail.
.TP
\f[CR]\-q\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-quiet\f[R]
Silence logs except for errors.
.SH SUPPORTED CONFIGURATION OPTIONS
.TP
\f[CR]config_dir\f[R]
Directory where Flox should load its configuration file (default:
\f[CR]$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/flox\f[R]).
This option will only take effect if set with
\f[CR]$FLOX_CONFIG_DIR\f[R].
\f[CR]config_dir\f[R] is ignored.
.TP
\f[CR]cache_dir\f[R]
Directory where Flox should store ephemeral data (default:
\f[CR]$XDG_CACHE_HOME/flox\f[R]).
.TP
\f[CR]data_dir\f[R]
Directory where Flox should store persistent data (default:
\f[CR]$XDG_DATA_HOME/flox\f[R]).
.TP
\f[CR]disable_hook\f[R]
Don\(cqt set up the Flox prompt hook as part of activation.
The prompt hook is required for \f[CR]flox deactivate\f[R] to take
effect (default: false).
.TP
\f[CR]disable_metrics\f[R]
Disable collecting and sending usage metrics.
.TP
\f[CR]floxhub_token\f[R]
Token to authenticate on FloxHub.
.TP
\f[CR]hide_default_prompt\f[R]
Hide environments named `default' from the shell prompt, and don\(cqt
add environments named `default' to \f[CR]$FLOX_PROMPT_ENVIRONMENTS\f[R]
(default: true).
.TP
\f[CR]installer_channel\f[R]
Release channel to use when checking for updates to Flox.
Valid values are \f[CR]stable\f[R], \f[CR]nightly\f[R], or
\f[CR]qa\f[R].
(default: \f[CR]stable\f[R])
.TP
\f[CR]search_limit\f[R]
How many items \f[CR]flox search\f[R] should show by default.
.TP
\f[CR]set_prompt\f[R]
Set shell prompt when activating an environment (default: true).
.TP
\f[CR]shell_prompt\f[R] \- DEPRECATED
Rule whether to change the shell prompt in activated environments
(default: \f[CR]show\-all\f[R]).
This has been deprecated in favor of \f[CR]set_prompt\f[R] and
\f[CR]hide_default_prompt\f[R].
Possible values are:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]show\-all\f[R]: shows all active environments
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]hide\-all\f[R]: disables the modification of the shell prompt
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]hide\-default\f[R]: filters out environments named
\f[CR]default\f[R] from the shell prompt
.RE
.TP
\f[CR]state_dir\f[R]
Directory where Flox should store data that\(cqs not critical but also
shouldn\(cqt be able to be freely deleted like data in the cache
directory.
(default: \f[CR]$XDG_STATE_HOME/flox\f[R]
e.g.\ \f[CR]\(ti/.local/state/flox\f[R])
.TP
\f[CR]trusted_environments\f[R]
Remote environments that are trusted for activation.
Contains keys of the form \f[CR]\(dq<owner>/<name>\(dq\f[R] that map to
either \f[CR]\(dqtrust\(dq\f[R] or \f[CR]\(dqdeny\(dq\f[R].
.TP
\f[CR]upgrade_notifications\f[R]
Print notification if upgrades are available on
\f[CR]flox activate\f[R].
The notification message is:
.RS
.IP
.EX
Upgrades are available for packages in \(aqenvironment\-name\(aq.
Use \(aqflox upgrade \-\-dry\-run\(aq for details.
.EE
.PP
(default: true)
.RE
.TP
\f[CR]keep_tempdir\f[R]
Flox creates a single tempdir for each process in
.PD 0
.P
.PD
\f[CR]$FLOX_CACHE_HOME/process\f[R].
.PD 0
.P
.PD
Flox will delete this tempdir upon conclusion of the process unless
\f[CR]keep_tempdir == true\f[R] AND verbose logs are enabled.
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
\f[CR]$FLOX_DISABLE_METRICS\f[R]
Variable for disabling the collection/sending of metrics data.
If set to \f[CR]true\f[R], prevents Flox from submitting basic metrics
information such as a unique token and the subcommand issued.
